<section class="membergroup-section">
  <h2 class="membergroup-title">my group</h2>

  <div class="membergroup-card">
    <p class="membergroup-intro">
      To join Twennie as a group, you need <strong>one leader</strong> and <strong>at least two group members</strong>.
    </p>

    <p class="membergroup-text">
      Group membership gives your team a shared learning environment. Leaders can guide development, assign learning, track progress, and help turn good intentions into visible action.
    </p>

    <p class="membergroup-text">
      As a group member, you can participate in team learning, receive assigned prompt sets and learning units, contribute to a shared custom library, and take part in missions and nuggets that help your team learn, investigate, and act together.
    </p>

    <p class="membergroup-text">
      This structure is especially useful for firms and teams that want to build stronger habits around learning, business development, knowledge sharing, and accountability.
    </p>

    <div class="membergroup-benefits">
      <h3 class="membergroup-benefits-title">group member benefits include:</h3>
      <ul class="membergroup-benefits-list">
        <li>access to a shared group learning environment</li>
        <li>leader-assigned learning and prompt sets</li>
        <li>progress tracking and completions</li>
        <li>shared missions and nuggets</li>
        <li>contributions to a team library</li>
        <li>greater accountability and coordination</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="membergroup-note">
      <p>
        If your team is interested in group access, Twennie can be organized around a designated leader who supports and coordinates the experience.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>